{
  "_comment": [
    "Exercise catalogue for Log Workout, the dashboard and the BigQuery roll-up. Edited by scripts/sync_exercises.py and the monthly programme sync.",
    "Only Olympic lifts (Snatch, Clean & Jerk) and their derivatives are logged by name. Everything else is logged under the muscle group it was captured under on the original data capture sheet ('Leg, Quads', 'Upper Body, Chest', ...).",
    "kind is 'olympic' or 'muscle_group'.",
    "Names must survive BigQuery INITCAP() unchanged and contain no '/', which would break /api/charts/{exercise_group}.",
    "aliases maps any other name (a programme spelling, a retired exercise, an old sheet value) to its catalogue entry. sql/01_stg_workouts.sql rolls history up with the same map; run 'python scripts/sync_exercises.py sql' after editing this file.",
    "one_rm_lifts are the club's tested 1RM lifts. one_rm_base says which lift's 1RM an Olympic derivative's % is taken from. one_rm_reference lists the 1RM lifts offered for a muscle group. Anything not listed uses its own 1RM."
  ],
